@inherits Custom.Hybrid.RazorTyped

<h1 @Kit.Toolbar.Default(MyItem)>
  Test app to verify that App Quality Tests
</h1>
<p>
  In 2sxc Apps-Dev we have a special app which manages the catalog of apps.

  An important feature of it is the "Quality Checks" which it can run on all these apps.

  This app is to verify that all the tests work as expected.
</p>
<blockquote>
  The way to use it is to create a file with a problem, and verify that it fails.
  Then fix the problem, and verify that it passes.
</blockquote>

<h2>We need this to:</h2>

<ol>
  <li>Ensure consistent quality of apps in the catalog, since they are usually used as examples for other developers and should therefore be of high quality.</li>
  <li>Ensure that we do not use old APIs that are being deprecated or phased out.</li>
  <li>Ensure that, as newer best practices are defined, we actually apply them and phase out outdated practices.</li>
</ol>

<p>
  Once apps have been fixed / updated, it can become unclear which checks actually still work,
  as we would notice tests if they simply don't test anything any more.

  So we need this special app which can simulate all issues,
  to verify the checks still work.
</p>

<h2>File Existence Examples</h2>

<ol>
  <li>You could rename the <code>app-icon.png</code> to something else, and an issue should trigger.</li>
  <li>Same for the <code>licenses.txt</code></li>
  <li>Also for the <code>App_Data/app.xml</code></li>
</ol>

<h2>App Configuration Examples</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Disable AJAX in the features</li>
  <li>Disable LightSpeed in the features</li>
  <li>Change the minimum 2sxc version</li>
  <li>Change the minimum DNN version</li>
  <li>Change the minimum Oqtane version</li>
  <li>
    Change LightSpeed, expected is 4h for users, 5m for editors, 5m for sysadmins. If you change it to something else, an issue should trigger.
    <code>
      &lt;Value Key="Title" Value="✅ - Users 14400s, Reg 🚫, Editors 300s, SysAdmins 300s" Type="String"&gt;
    </code>
  </li>
</ol>